//   BM=16, BN=16, BK=32
//   16×16 block (256 threads), each computes one output element.
//   BK=32 → one shared-mem tile per K-slice, giving 32 MACs per thread per
//           load → good compute/memory ratio.
//   Registers per thread ≈ 20 → 6 blocks/SM → 100 % occupancy.
//
//   33-padded shared memory (33 = 32+1, odd stride → no 32-bank conflicts).
// ============================================================================

