using namespace nvcuda;

// ============================================================================
// WMMA TF32 GEMM for A40 (sm_86, Ampere)
//
// Each block is 16x16 threads (256 threads, 8 warps).
// Each warp computes one 16x16 output tile using two 16x8 WMMA sub-tiles.
//
// Strategy:
//   - Shared-memory tiling with BM=BN=BK=32
//   - 1024-thread block (32x32), 1024 threads
//   - 2 k-slices per tile (BK=16 each)
//   - Each warp (32 threads) computes 16x8 using WMMA, two warps per tile
//     No, actually each warp handles 16x16 via two 16x8 tiles.
//   - With 1 block per SM (1024 threads): 1024/1536 = 67% occupancy
//   - Each warp computes 256 MACs per WMMA call (16*16*1)
//     Actually, 16x8x16 = 2048 MACs per WMMA mma_sync call.
//
// Actually: each warp has 32 threads. With 8 warps per block:
// - Each warp processes 16x8 output tile = 128 elements
// - 8 warps * 128 = 1024 elements = 32x32 output tile ✓
// - Each warp uses one 16x16 WMMA accumulator fragment
// - Two 16x8 WMMA loads for A and B tiles
